Thus we need to allocate dispatch slot for each candidate (origin, destination, shift_candidate_beta) using dispatch_slot_alpha. However note dispatch_slot_alpha can only be allocated to one candidate at a time because allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate removes dispatch_slot_available. After allocation, dispatch_slot_available becomes false. To allocate to another candidate, we would need to make it available again. There's no action that makes dispatch_slot_available except the execute_*_dispatch actions which have effect (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). So after we dispatch a candidate, the dispatch slot becomes available again. So we can allocate, then dispatch, then slot free for next.

Thus sequence: For each candidate, we need to make it dispatch_ready, allocate dispatch slot (consumes slot), then execute dispatch (which releases slot). After dispatch, we have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked still true (effect does not remove it). Good.

Thus we can do origin, destination, shift_candidate_beta sequentially.

